<!-- cm_07_ev.xml
     Current Measures: Boost Pakistan EV (BEV) technology share-weights.
     CONTEXT:
       EV Activity targets: 0.008 GWa (2025), 0.33 GWa (2030).
       Pakistan NDC: 30% EV by 2030.
       Baseline: BEV share-weight = 0 in 2025, s-curve to 1 by 2030 (global tech DB).
       With share-weight=0 in 2025, BEV cannot compete at all in that period.
     METHOD: Set BEV share-weight > 0 in 2025 to "turn on" EVs early.
             Boost to 2.0+ from 2030 onward to reflect 30% EV policy push.
             Applied to all three 4W subsectors (Car, Large Car and Truck, Mini Car)
             and 2W/3W subsector.
     SCOPE NOTE: GCAM "Final Energy|Transportation|LDV|Electricity" includes 2W/3W.
                 MESSAGE target may be 4W only. We boost both for CM.
     RISK: Medium. Transport sector has cost coupling through fuel markets and
           consumer durable tracking. BEV share-weight is at technology level
           (not subsector). Keep modest — iterate after first run.
     NOTE: If model fails, this module is safe to remove first (small sector).
-->
